    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-75962: exponential growth dominates logarithmic growth, so the limit is 0. q-123715: logarithms grow more slowly than positive powers, and powers grow more slowly than exponentials, so all three sequences converge to 0. q-117135 and q-117141: arccos decreases from (-1, pi) through (0, pi/2) to (1, 0), matching the selected image. q-117212 and q-70743: its domain is [-1,1], which excludes -pi/2 and includes 2/3. q-117221: its range is [0,pi], which includes 2. q-42433: its maximum point is (-1,pi). q-65828: only III satisfies x=cos(y) with y in [0,pi]; I has x>1, and II has y>pi. q-70769: only I satisfies these conditions; II has negative y, and III fails cos(pi/3)=1. q-10406: tangent requires x/3 to differ from pi/2+n*pi, giving the stated exclusions. q-81542: tan(2x)=0 exactly when 2x=n*pi, so all zeros are n*pi/2. q-43659 and q-117265: arctan is increasing through the origin with horizontal asymptotes at y=±pi/2, matching the selected image. q-70777 and q-117329: arctan has domain all real numbers, so all three listed values qualify in each question. No earlier submission or grade was supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematical verification.",
